/**
 * English dictionary, split into chunks, Oct 29, 2026.
 * Code 27, 2nd commit (Wilson: I like to type proper
 * English, so make sure all the words in the dictionary
 * are proper): cleaned from the original 20,143-word
 * frequency list down to 17395 words.
 * Cleaning rule, in order:
 * 1. Keep every word in a standard English dictionary
 *    (dwyl/english-words words_alpha.txt, 370,104 words).
 * 2. Keep the most common modern/tech/proper words from
 *    the original list even if that dictionary excludes
 *    them (website, blog, google, xbox, samsung, etc. —
 *    top 4,000 in original frequency order).
 * 3. Keep intentional additions no matter what: military
 *    ranks (including digit ranks like pv2, 1sg, and maj,
 *    which was missing before), contractions, eala,
 *    autocorrect, spacebar, swipe, tagalog.
 * 4. Two-letter words: only a curated list of real
 *    two-letter English words (it, is, go, ok, tv, etc.)
 *    plus rank abbreviations. This alone removes cj,
 *    kt, and 472 other two-letter fragments that the
 *    swipe matcher used to pick over real words.
 * 5. Removed: fragments, truncations (econo), foreign
 *    words (zoofilia, verzeichnis, zum), and porn terms
 *    (milf, hentai, shemale, etc.). If Wilson types a
 *    removed word himself, his personal dictionary
 *    learns it after a couple of uses, so nothing he
 *    actually types is lost for good.
 * Split into one object per chunk on purpose: a single
 * listOf with this many arguments would blow the JVM
 * 64KB method-size limit for its initializer. Each chunk
 * object has its own small initializer; Dictionary.WORDS
 * just concatenates them.
 */

